<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yugoslavia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yugoslav state</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yugoslavia was a state of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, proclaimed in 1918 as the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> from territories including former Austro-Hungarian lands. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> list it among the successor states of the empire. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it was invaded and partly occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yugoslavia.jpg" alt="Yugoslavia" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: of History_of_Yugoslavia.svg by NikNaks Portions used contain parts of: Blank_map_of_Europe_1929-1938.svg and … · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yugoslavia_location_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
